+Pilot evidence supplement: s-core_sw_fabric
+-----------------------------------------
+
+This section supplements the proposed decision in issue
+`3115 <https://github.com/eclipse-score/score/issues/3115>`_. It records one
+exploratory integration, not an accepted toolchain selection or qualification.
+
+Context
+~~~~~~~
+
+S-CORE already owns the engineering process, work-product definitions and
+Sphinx-Needs metamodel. The integration question is how AI assistance works
+within those rules with traceability, bounded context, measured verification
+and accountable human review. Replacing that process with a second framework's
+artifact authority would require additional synchronization and review.
+
+The review asks for real experience, lifecycle loopbacks, manageable agent
+context and qualification evidence. The s-core_sw_fabric pilot supplies
+implementation experience; alternatives inspected only through documentation
+remain untested. Its source is identified by commit
+``7e24a43c258f1dcaa2b27e02b501964847bc8714`` plus a captured dirty working tree,
+including selected untracked code, controls and tests. The packet has per-file
+hashes, historical measurements, licenses and explicit replay boundaries.
+
+Proposed decision
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Evaluate the tooling by layer and execute a bounded native-process pilot
+before organization-wide selection. Keep native S-CORE semantics and IDs
+authoritative; derive context and sidecar graphs from pinned native sources.
+Use Spec Kit to develop the integration, while native S-CORE products retain
+their native formats. Evaluate packaging separately from execution. Agents
+can draft and critique; deterministic tools measure checks; authorized humans
+make the required engineering decisions outside unattended workflows.
+
+Evidence and limits
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+* Spec Kit v1.0.12 at ``e77daa9021d20db26b878f7dfa5640fe5a42d04e`` was used for
+  fabric development. Native catalogue, artifact trace, impact, freshness,
+  MCP context, selected skills and evidence-refresh implementations exist.
+  This does not establish organization-wide native-task adoption.
+* Historical 011 logs retain 2,056 passed tests and 22 skips, plus 139 passing
+  affected-scope checks and the original failing attempt. These results
+  belong to their recorded subjects, not the current dirty snapshot.
+* Context experiments distinguish synthetic byte estimates (86.94--95.12%),
+  initial live rendering proxies (30.46--30.63%) and later tool-projection
+  rendering proxies (66.32--66.60%). Expected fixture outputs stayed equal.
+  Real engineering-task savings, semantic adequacy, billing and runtime
+  improvement remain unestablished.
+* The retained lifecycle #704 packet includes a scoped implementation and
+  113 passing native cases. A historical DeepSeek communication #1261 attempt
+  retained compilation failure and zero of five executed tests despite
+  orchestration completion; later Claude correction evidence retains passing
+  selected Linux checks. Qualification and upstream acceptance remain separate.
+* Disposable MCP probes and native Fabro runtime probes are retained. APM
+  packaging installation/rollout is not measured here. The pinned Fabro
+  candidate did not provide working same-run checkpoint resume.
+* Production trust roots, approved applicability/check denominators and
+  qualified engineering authority remain open. Fixture gates and tests do
+  not establish ASIL-B qualification or native engineering acceptance.
+
+All eight issue-listed options are covered in the accompanying assessment:
+APM, Lola and OKIT for packaging; Syspilot, BMAD, Spec Kit and Pharaoh for
+SDLC/harness; Harbor for evaluation. The seven alternatives to the measured
+Spec Kit development experience have revision-bound primary-source research,
+not head-to-head executions. The Pharaoh URL redirects to an archived skills
+repository; successor support requires a separate assessment.
+
+Consequences
+~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The proposal keeps one engineering authority and allows independent tool
+selection, at the cost of explicit compatibility, provenance, retention and
+review work. Changed requirements must trigger renewed impact and evidence
+assessment. Missing or unsupported checks remain visible. A runtime success
+cannot authorize artifact acceptance or tool qualification.
+
+The proposed supplement requires maintainer review, agreed comparative pilot
+scope, reconciliation with the current native DR template and category layout,
+and native documentation CI. The original decision-record ID and proposed
+status remain unchanged by this supplement. No accepting person, decision date
+or approval is inferred from measurements.
